nce 2000, Fort Myers has set <strong class=\"sig\">25 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 78 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">118 record highs</strong>, far more than the 77 that chance alone would give. The 1980s hold the most record highs of any decade (70). Fort Myers' all-time high is 103\u00b0F, on June 16, 1981.","t_chg":"Fort Myers has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 116 complete years: Fort Myers' average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.24\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.18 to +0.30), about +3.1\u00b0F since 1892. Fort Myers' average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.27\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.21 to +0.33), about +3.6\u00b0F since 1892.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Fort Myers' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.46 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 57.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 2024 (80.45 in); the driest, 1964 (32.83 in). Fort Myers almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 10 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}